%erg 0.1
Title: erg new should parse --author and reject unknown flags
Created: 2026-05-29
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-05-29T19:15Z Claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Found while creating a ticket during the 0165 CI work. Running

    erg new "Some title" --author Claude

silently created a stray `./--author/` directory and dropped the value
`Claude`. Cause: `cmdNew` (src/go/new.go) treats `args[0]` as TITLE and
`args[1]` as DIR with no flag parsing — so `--author` became the DIR
positional (passed through `os.MkdirAll`) and the following token was
ignored.

Two defects:

1. **No `--author` flag.** Author is only resolvable via `$ERG_AUTHOR`,
   git `user.name`, or `$USER`. There is no per-invocation override, even
   though the help text frames author as a first-class field.
2. **Unknown flags are not rejected.** Any `-`-prefixed token that isn't a
   positional is silently consumed as DIR, so a typo (`--athor`, `--dir`)
   becomes a created directory rather than an error. This is a data-safety
   footgun: `erg` is meant never to surprise the user with stray writes.

`src/go/rm.go` already establishes the house convention: a switch over
known flags, a `default` that rejects unknown `-`-prefixed tokens and
collects positionals.

## Relevant files

- `src/go/new.go` — `cmdNew` arg parsing, `helpNew`, usage strings
- `src/go/identity.go` — `resolveAuthor`; factor out the newline-sanitizer
  so a `--author` value gets the same anti-injection hardening
- `src/go/new_test.go` — add coverage
- `tests/test_new.sh` — CLI-level coverage

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg new TITLE --author NAME` (and `-a NAME`, `--author=NAME`) sets
      the Author header
- [ ] An explicit `--author` overrides the env/git/USER chain
- [ ] A `--author` value is newline-sanitized (no header injection); an
      empty value is an error, not a silent fallback
- [ ] Unknown `-`-prefixed flags are rejected with a non-zero exit and a
      usage message — NOT turned into a DIR
- [ ] `erg new TITLE DIR` (positional store) still works unchanged
- [ ] `helpNew` / usage strings document `--author`
- [ ] Go unit + `tests/test_new.sh` coverage for the above
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Notes

Do NOT implement in the 0165 branch/worktree — this is its own ticket and
must be isolated in its own worktree (`/start-ticket 166`).
